(Code 1977, § 24-4; Ord. No. 88-16, § 2, 6-7-1988)

935:
(a) Any transient merchant shall submit evidence with his license application showing that such transient merchant has filed with the city clerk the name and permanent address of the transient merchant's registered agent. Such agent shall be a local property owner and a resident of the county for the previous 12 months. It shall be the responsibility of this individual to act as agent of such transient merchant upon whom any process, notice, or demand required or permitted by law to be served upon the transient merchant may be served in the same manner provided by law for the service of a summons or complaint. Said registered agent shall agree in writing to act as such agent, and a copy of the agreement shall be filed with the license application. In addition, such registered agent must be of such character and integrity as to be bondable.
(b) Any such registered agent shall act in the same capacity and have the same duties and responsibilities, and be subject to the same actions of the superior court, as would any agent registered as required by O.C.G.A. § 43-46-1 et seq., known as the "Transient Merchant Act of Georgia."
(c) In addition, all registered agents shall also complete an application containing the following information and file such with the city before any license shall be issued to a transient merchant:
(1) Name of registered agent;
(2) Permanent address and phone number of registered agent;
(3) Length of time that registered agent has been a resident of the county;
(4) Location of property owned by this individual which would qualify one to act as a registered agent.
Such application shall be signed under oath by the registered agent.
(Code 1977, § 24-5; Ord. No. 88-16, § 2, 6-7-1988)

945:
